    (v_topic_id, 'Patient #60773: An 12-year-old overweight adolescent undergoes in situ pinning for a stable Slipped Capital Femoral Epiphysis (SCFE). At follow-up, the patient complains of severe stiffness and loss of joint space is noted on X-ray. What is this devastating complication?', '["Chondrolysis", "Infection", "Avascular necrosis of the femoral head", "Heterotopic ossification", "Nonunion"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Detailed orthopedic assessment of the pediatric patient is required to identify these specific conditions correctly and avoid serious long-term complications.'),
